1
00:00:32,159 --> 00:00:34,000
Sir, please take a seat over here.

2
00:00:35,719 --> 00:00:36,280
Okay.

3
00:00:44,880 --> 00:00:47,119
How are things between you two right now?

4
00:00:49,399 --> 00:00:50,679
That's not the point.

5
00:00:51,399 --> 00:00:52,159
I'm sorry.

6
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,039
This part is very important.

7
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:57,880
So your feelings for your wife...

8
00:00:57,880 --> 00:00:58,799
haven't changed at all?

9
00:00:58,880 --> 00:00:59,399
No.

10
00:01:04,719 --> 00:01:07,000
How long has it been since you were intimate?

11
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:09,159
That... That's not the point.

12
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:10,920
This is very important.

13
00:01:11,799 --> 00:01:13,040
We agreed

14
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,760
to be honest with each other.

15
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:17,640
Not since then.

16
00:01:19,239 --> 00:01:20,079
Why is that?

17
00:01:21,159 --> 00:01:21,959
It's just...

18
00:01:21,959 --> 00:01:24,000
It's because...

19
00:01:25,359 --> 00:01:26,280
I get scared.

20
00:01:26,719 --> 00:01:27,719
Scared of losing again.

21
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:36,560
Have you considered having another child?

22
00:01:48,840 --> 00:01:50,239
Yes, yes.

23
00:01:50,599 --> 00:01:52,680
What made you consider

24
00:01:53,519 --> 00:01:54,599
having another one?

25
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,640
With this whole thing...

26
00:01:57,760 --> 00:01:59,319
maybe we could... could move past it.

27
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:01,760
Because...

28
00:02:02,519 --> 00:02:06,079
that's exactly where the root problem lies.

29
00:02:08,120 --> 00:02:09,560
Can I speak to you in private?

30
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:12,639
Is that okay?

31
00:02:17,280 --> 00:02:18,439
Sorry, um...

32
00:02:18,439 --> 00:02:19,639
could you step out for a moment?

33
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,680
I'm sorry.

34
00:02:51,719 --> 00:02:53,120
Aren't you going to hit me?

35
00:02:54,840 --> 00:02:56,000
Why would I hit you

36
00:02:57,639 --> 00:02:58,520
to punish you?

37
00:02:59,639 --> 00:03:00,479
Go ahead.

38
00:03:01,919 --> 00:03:03,800
Hit me wherever you want.

39
00:03:04,879 --> 00:03:05,840
How did we

40
00:03:07,039 --> 00:03:08,400
end up like this?

41
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:34,240
Have you been waiting long?

42
00:03:34,400 --> 00:03:36,960
I just met with a client.

43
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,520
Okay, let's order... order something.

44
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:44,280
No, it's fine. No need.

45
00:03:46,840 --> 00:03:47,879
How long have you been back?

46
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,039
A couple of days.

47
00:03:52,400 --> 00:03:53,280
How's Mom?

48
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:55,360
She's fine. Everything's good.

49
00:03:56,039 --> 00:03:57,439
Didn't you say you had something urgent?

50
00:03:57,439 --> 00:03:58,319
What is it?

51
00:04:02,919 --> 00:04:04,120
I was thinking...

52
00:04:05,560 --> 00:04:07,319
let's get a divorce if there's really no other way.

53
00:04:09,639 --> 00:04:11,919
"Really no other way"...

54
00:04:14,639 --> 00:04:16,000
Why phrase it like that?

55
00:04:16,199 --> 00:04:18,120
I... I don't want this either.

56
00:04:19,519 --> 00:04:20,279
But...

57
00:04:22,560 --> 00:04:24,800
we just can't solve this problem right now.

58
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:27,959
You... you keep saying it yourself.

59
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:31,920
You always think of him.

60
00:04:33,519 --> 00:04:34,639
Don't you?

61
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:36,040
I do.

62
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:40,480
That's why I said we can't solve this.

63
00:04:42,759 --> 00:04:46,079
This is the only option we have left.

64
00:04:47,079 --> 00:04:48,000
On my end,

65
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:51,560
I've... I've tried everything I could.

66
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,319
Tried

67
00:04:56,079 --> 00:04:57,160
to do what?

68
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:02,240
I...

69
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:05,279
I've been explaining it to you.

70
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:10,000
I've been trying to lay out

71
00:05:10,720 --> 00:05:13,600
the whole story clearly for you.

72
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:16,399
I've been analyzing it for you.

73
00:05:19,199 --> 00:05:22,000
Yeah, you explained it very clearly.

74
00:05:23,279 --> 00:05:24,480
And analyzed it very thoroughly.

75
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:32,519
Okay, I agree.

76
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:39,680
You... you agree to...

77
00:05:40,279 --> 00:05:41,360
I agree to the divorce.

78
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:47,279
So you...

79
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:51,839
think that I did something wrong?

80
00:05:53,879 --> 00:05:54,680
No.

81
00:05:57,519 --> 00:05:58,480
You were perfect.

82
00:06:16,120 --> 00:06:17,439
What's wrong with your voice?

83
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:20,480
My voice?

84
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,399
It's hoarse.

85
00:06:24,160 --> 00:06:26,079
You sound like Donald Duck.

86
00:06:42,959 --> 00:06:43,839
Dr. Li.

87
00:06:45,040 --> 00:06:46,319
We asked you here today

88
00:06:46,319 --> 00:06:47,759
mainly to ask you a few things.

89
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,839
When Xie Xin and his wife were in your office,

90
00:06:49,839 --> 00:06:50,680
what did you talk about?

91
00:06:50,720 --> 00:06:51,639
What happened?

92
00:06:57,279 --> 00:06:59,920
They came for relationship counseling.

93
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:02,600
Let me explain.

94
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:06,680
We did run into a few minor issues back then

95
00:07:07,639 --> 00:07:10,519
in our marriage.

96
00:07:10,519 --> 00:07:13,519
It's normal for couples to have issues.

97
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:15,639
Xie Xin was busy.

98
00:07:15,879 --> 00:07:18,160
We did communicate less.

99
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:19,920
So we went to see Dr. Li

100
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:22,160
for some relationship counseling.

101
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:25,879
It's true. We hadn't for a long time...

102
00:07:27,560 --> 00:07:30,720
We hadn't sat down for a proper talk, right?

103
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:34,839
Right, right.

104
00:07:35,240 --> 00:07:36,560
And what was this minor issue?

105
00:07:37,079 --> 00:07:40,160
They had a child before.

106
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:44,199
A child?

107
00:07:50,439 --> 00:07:52,240
Yes, yes.

108
00:07:52,600 --> 00:07:54,560
We did have a child.

109
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:56,160
We did.

110
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:59,160
Since it was my first pregnancy,

111
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:00,680
I wasn't very careful.

112
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,279
I ate lots of raw and cold food, and...

113
00:08:04,160 --> 00:08:06,000
sadly, I ended up in the hospital.

114
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:06,959
How did you get there?

115
00:08:07,439 --> 00:08:08,560
We took a car.

116
00:08:08,560 --> 00:08:09,040
We drove.

117
00:08:09,040 --> 00:08:09,480
Who drove the car?

118
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:10,000
I did... No.

119
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,519
I drove.

120
00:08:10,519 --> 00:08:11,079
No, Xie Xin.

121
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:12,000
I had a bit to drink.

122
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:12,879
You're remembering it wrong.

123
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,160
That day was...

124
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:15,399
our wedding anniversary.

125
00:08:15,399 --> 00:08:17,199
And we were having such a wonderful time

126
00:08:17,199 --> 00:08:18,879
at a really beautiful restaurant, right?

127
00:08:19,079 --> 00:08:20,720
You even ordered a steak for me,

128
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:21,639
and some cake.

129
00:08:21,759 --> 00:08:23,240
And we were so, so happy that day.

130
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:23,879
And then...

131
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,560
my... my stomach started hurting.

132
00:08:25,560 --> 00:08:26,800
And I had a little to drink.

133
00:08:26,800 --> 00:08:27,360
No, no.

134
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,560
Xie Xin, you're really remembering it wrong.

135
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:29,920
It was... it was that delivery rider.

136
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:31,480
That delivery rider ran a red light.

137
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,399
That's why we...

138
00:08:32,399 --> 00:08:33,480
But if I hadn't been drinking,

139
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,120
I could have reacted in time. No.

140
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:34,960
It had nothing to do with that!

141
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:36,200
Xie Xin. Xie Xin!

142
00:08:36,200 --> 00:08:36,919
Listen to me.

143
00:08:36,919 --> 00:08:37,840
It wasn't like that.

144
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:38,759
It wasn't like that.

145
00:08:38,759 --> 00:08:40,240
He clearly ran the red light!

146
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:42,120
Okay, okay, okay.

147
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:43,480
Xie Xin.

148
00:08:43,480 --> 00:08:45,200
Let me explain, okay?

149
00:08:52,200 --> 00:08:54,519
Come, come, come here. Come.

150
00:08:56,559 --> 00:08:57,879
Let me explain.

151
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,679
The wedding anniversary was...

152
00:08:59,679 --> 00:09:02,679
It really was our anniversary. We also had...

153
00:09:03,159 --> 00:09:04,240
a delicious steak.

154
00:09:04,240 --> 00:09:05,559
Just like my Honey said.

155
00:09:05,559 --> 00:09:08,159
And I did have some to drink.

156
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:10,039
But because my Honey was

157
00:09:10,039 --> 00:09:10,960
having such bad stomach pains,

158
00:09:10,960 --> 00:09:13,639
I didn't call a sober driver service.

159
00:09:13,639 --> 00:09:16,799
I insisted on driving her to the hospital myself.

160
00:09:17,720 --> 00:09:19,240
We hit the delivery rider.

161
00:09:19,320 --> 00:09:21,240
I slammed on the brakes.

162
00:09:21,480 --> 00:09:23,320
When I looked at her again,

163
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,440
her...

164
00:09:26,039 --> 00:09:31,919
her dress was already covered in red.

165
00:09:33,159 --> 00:09:35,440
When we got to the hospital...

166
00:09:35,679 --> 00:09:37,120
Yeah, right.

167
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,360
Then what is the real reason for the divorce?

168
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,960
Why divorce? Why get a divorce?

169
00:10:02,639 --> 00:10:03,799
You're being a bit too good to me.

170
00:10:04,039 --> 00:10:04,879
Let me just say this.

171
00:10:08,440 --> 00:10:11,240
You have no idea how the people before chewed me out.

172
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:16,000
Still saving face for me, really.

173
00:10:16,480 --> 00:10:17,639
You really do know me.

174
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:22,799
The thing is... I

175
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:25,879
am someone who easily

176
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,919
runs away or, let's say,

177
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:31,000
avoids problems.

178
00:10:31,360 --> 00:10:34,080
Throughout my life, it's always been

179
00:10:34,080 --> 00:10:36,840
my Honey who tolerates and guides me.

180
00:10:37,039 --> 00:10:38,519
She treats me really well.

181
00:10:38,639 --> 00:10:40,039
About this divorce thing,

182
00:10:40,039 --> 00:10:42,039
I actually said it was about the child then.

183
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:42,720
But...

184
00:10:42,960 --> 00:10:45,600
Are you afraid someone can't hear or what?

185
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,840
Turn this up for me.

186
00:10:51,919 --> 00:10:53,080
About the divorce,

187
00:10:54,679 --> 00:10:56,360
I... I lied to you.

188
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,799
What I said back then was

189
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,519
I couldn't... I... I couldn't face the child.

190
00:11:03,720 --> 00:11:07,960
But actually, it's because I couldn't face

191
00:11:09,279 --> 00:11:11,840
the fact that it seemed I caused

192
00:11:11,840 --> 00:11:14,399
this outcome.

193
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:19,720
So I... I owe you an apology.

194
00:11:25,519 --> 00:11:26,440
I'm sorry, Honey.

195
00:11:31,679 --> 00:11:33,480
Are you going to hit me or what?

196
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,200
Are you going to...

197
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:17,759
Having fun?

198
00:13:19,159 --> 00:13:19,759
I am.

199
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:25,120
What's the score?

200
00:13:28,480 --> 00:13:29,840
Ten to twelve.

201
00:13:31,279 --> 00:13:31,919
Okay.

202
00:13:33,559 --> 00:13:34,360
Come on, Honey.

203
00:13:35,799 --> 00:13:36,720
Do you want to get shocked?

204
00:13:37,919 --> 00:13:38,759
Not really, actually.

205
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:39,559
I'm a bit tired.

206
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,919
But I don't want you getting shocked either.

207
00:13:44,120 --> 00:13:44,679
Alright.

208
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:45,799
Come on.

209
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:55,679
I forfeit.

210
00:14:11,600 --> 00:14:14,000
Zhang Ya chose to forfeit.

211
00:14:14,639 --> 00:14:17,360
There are no losers in this round.

212
00:14:20,879 --> 00:14:23,039
And no one will be punished.

213
00:14:23,720 --> 00:14:24,679
No, you are.

214
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:26,120
You're not just a Psycho,

215
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,879
you're also a liar.

216
00:14:28,519 --> 00:14:29,559
Why didn't you tell me this rule earlier?

217
00:14:29,559 --> 00:14:30,519
I got beaten up like this,

218
00:14:30,519 --> 00:14:31,519
and shocked so many times.

219
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:33,360
If I knew, I could've just done that.

220
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:34,600
Whatever, forget it.

221
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:35,759
Didn't you have five people?

222
00:14:35,919 --> 00:14:37,960
Hurry up, bring the other two up.

223
00:14:38,279 --> 00:14:41,120
So far, Old Lin, my bro, my Honey.

224
00:14:41,279 --> 00:14:42,080
Who else?

225
00:14:42,399 --> 00:14:43,759
Could it be my parents?

226
00:14:43,759 --> 00:14:44,759
You even ordered takeout?

227
00:14:44,759 --> 00:14:45,759
You won't have time to eat it.

228
00:14:45,879 --> 00:14:47,559
I'm wrapping this up quickly.

229
00:14:48,879 --> 00:14:49,360
Bro, you...

230
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:50,080
No, don't come up here.

231
00:14:50,080 --> 00:14:50,879
Leave it at the door.

232
00:14:50,879 --> 00:14:51,879
Leave it at the door. It's dangerous here.

233
00:14:51,879 --> 00:14:52,799
It's all electrified.

234
00:14:52,799 --> 00:14:54,279
You... hurry up and get down.

235
00:14:54,799 --> 00:14:55,919
Next person. Name.

236
00:14:57,159 --> 00:14:57,960
Wang Ke.

237
00:14:58,320 --> 00:14:59,960
Okay, Wang Ke. Never heard of him.

238
00:15:00,919 --> 00:15:02,000
I am Wang Ke.

239
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Do we know each other?
